{"type":"message","timestamp":"2026-06-11T11:40:10.886Z","role":"user","content":"You are a Gemini worker on `underrated` (an independent web browser engine in Rust, edition 2024). Work and respond in English.\nFirst, read the entire AGENTS.md passed via --include-directories and follow all of it (esp. I-1..I-7).\n\nTask: t0265 — expose `value` get/set on form-control elements (input/textarea/select/option/button) as a JS DOM binding, reflecting the `value` content attribute\nRead: docs/SPEC.md (script/DOM section) and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md under /workspaces/underrated-meta/\nTarget module: src/script/ (touch ONLY src/script/mod.rs; do NOT touch other modules or other worktrees)\n\nContext: In src/script/mod.rs, the DOM node prototype already reflects content attributes via Object.defineProperty.\nFor example `className` is defined as:\n  Object.defineProperty(node, 'className', { get(){ return this.getAttribute('class') || ''; },\n                                             set(v){ this.setAttribute('class', String(v)); },\n                                             enumerable: true, configurable: true });\nand `id` is defined analogously. The working `getAttribute`/`setAttribute` bridge methods already exist.\nThere is currently NO `value` property (grep confirms 0 occurrences of 'value' as a defined property), so JS like\n`document.querySelector('input').value` and `el.value = 'hello'` do not work. This is on the MVP critical path\n(reading/writing the search box before a form submit navigation).\n\nApproach: test-first (TDD). Implement entirely inside src/script/mod.rs by adding a `value` accessor on the node\nprototype, exactly mirroring the existing `className`/`id` defineProperty pattern:\n  - get value(): returns `this.getAttribute('value') || ''`\n  - set value(v): calls `this.setAttribute('value', String(v))`\n  All read/write (getter+setter), enumerable: true, configurable: true.\n\nIMPORTANT scope/spec note: In the full HTML spec, `input.value` is governed by a \"dirty value flag\" and is NOT a pure\nreflection of the `value` content attribute (typing diverges the IDL value from the attribute). We are intentionally\nimplementing the simpler **content-attribute reflection** first (consistent with this engine's static-render model).\nAdd a `// TODO(spec): input.value dirty-value-flag / live IDL value vs content attribute (see HTML spec)` comment next\nto the accessor, and do NOT attempt to implement the dirty-value-flag behavior in this task.\n\nAcceptance (must be green) — add Rust #[test] cases in src/script/mod.rs mirroring the existing style (eval_with_dom):\n  1. An <input> that has a `value` attribute exposes it via `.value` (get returns the attribute string).\n  2. An element with no `value` attribute returns the empty string `''` from `.value` (not undefined/null).\n  3. Setting `el.value = 'hello'` makes `el.getAttribute('value') === 'hello'` and a subsequent `el.value === 'hello'`.\n  4. Setting a non-string (e.g. a number) coerces via String() — `el.value = 42; el.value === '42'`.\n  Build the elements using the existing test helpers (document.createElement / getElementById), consistent with the\n  other accessor tests in this file.\n\nDone when: `cargo test && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo fmt --check` all pass.\nCommit: `feat(script): expose value get/set reflecting the value attribute on form controls (t0265)`.\nComments and identifiers in English. Do NOT skip/ignore tests (I-4). No unwrap/expect in non-test body code (I-6).\nTouch ONLY src/script/mod.rs — do NOT modify src/dom, src/html, or any other module or worktree.\nIMPORTANT: git add + git commit your work on the current branch BEFORE finishing (do not leave changes uncommitted).\nIf the spec is ambiguous or conflicts with real browser behavior beyond the note above, do NOT decide on your own —\nleave `// TODO(spec):` and report.\nEnd with a short summary of what changed."}
